# Attaches the correct Meta Llama 3 Instruct chat template to the
# already-pulled OpenBioLLM-Llama3-8B Q4_K_M GGUF, which embeds no usable
# template of its own.
#
# Verified directly: `ollama show
# hf.co/aaditya/OpenBioLLM-Llama3-8B-GGUF:Q4_K_M --modelfile` reports only
# `TEMPLATE {{ .Prompt }}`, a bare passthrough with no role/turn
# structure. A manual test against that untemplated import asked it to
# extract a medication from a plain clinical sentence, and it
# reformulated the request as a question instead of answering it.
# OpenBioLLM's own model card requires the exact Llama 3 Instruct
# template for correct behavior, since it is a fine-tune of
# Meta-Llama-3-8B-Instruct that was never retrained with a different
# conversational format.
#
# FROM reuses the exact GGUF/quantization already pulled via
# `ollama pull hf.co/aaditya/OpenBioLLM-Llama3-8B-GGUF:Q4_K_M`. `ollama
# create` attaches a new template/parameters to that existing blob; it
# does not re-download or modify the underlying weights.
FROM hf.co/aaditya/OpenBioLLM-Llama3-8B-GGUF:Q4_K_M

# --- Meta Llama 3 Instruct chat template ---------------------------------
# Copied verbatim, unmodified, from Ollama's own official `llama3` library
# model (`ollama pull llama3:8b-instruct-q4_K_M && ollama show
# llama3:8b-instruct-q4_K_M --modelfile`) - the authoritative reference
# for this architecture's intended prompt format. If this ever needs
# revisiting, re-derive it from that same source rather than hand-editing
# the block below.
TEMPLATE """{{ if .System }}<|start_header_id|>system<|end_header_id|>

{{ .System }}<|eot_id|>{{ end }}{{ if .Prompt }}<|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>

{{ .Prompt }}<|eot_id|>{{ end }}<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>

{{ .Response }}<|eot_id|>"""

# Also copied verbatim from the same reference Modelfile.
#
# num_keep: how many leading tokens are protected from eviction if the
# context needs mid-generation truncation/shifting once the context
# window fills up. This is a context-management setting, not part of
# chat-template rendering (that's the TEMPLATE block above), so it has no
# bearing on the correctness fix this file exists for. Retained anyway,
# unchanged, for byte-for-byte fidelity to the known-good reference
# config; it is harmless here regardless, since MedLens's benchmark
# prompts are short, single-turn, and nowhere near this model's context
# limit, so no mid-generation truncation is ever expected to occur.
PARAMETER num_keep 24
PARAMETER stop <|start_header_id|>
PARAMETER stop <|end_header_id|>
PARAMETER stop <|eot_id|>

# Deliberately no SYSTEM directive: MedLens sends a single user-turn
# message with no system prompt (see openbiollm_provider.py), and this
# file must not introduce a MedLens- or OpenBioLLM-specific system prompt
# the benchmark task doesn't define.
